# Byte-exact trees: nothing here may be line-ending normalized on the way into
# or out of the index.
#
# Every file under these paths is hashed by the tool and pinned by a digest
# literal in the test suite -- a contract source bound by `contract.source_sha256`
# and quoted byte-for-byte by `source_span`, an evidence artifact whose sha256
# reaches a receipt, or a frozen copy of both that reproduces a receipt digest
# issued by an earlier version.
#
# Measured in a sibling repository on 2026-09-09: with `core.autocrlf=input` and
# no `.gitattributes`, `git add` wrote a blob with the carriage returns stripped
# while the worktree file still hashed to the recorded digest. The gate was green
# locally and would have failed on every fresh clone, on a byte no tool touched.
# None of these files carries a CR today; the point is that a contributor with a
# different `core.autocrlf` cannot introduce or remove one silently.
/examples/** -text
/tests/fixtures/** -text
